 Vedmich`],affiliation:`Sr. Solutions Architect, AWS`},{start:`11:00`,end:`11:15`,title:`Why dbt Exists: Cheap Cloud Storage, the Death of ETL, and the Analytics Engineer`,description:`Trace how cheap cloud storage shifted data pipelines from ETL to ELT, creating the need for dbt and analytics engineering. See how S3, Athena, Redshift and dbt fit together in an AWS data stack, then learn practical steps for building the skills and preparing for interviews in this field.`,speakers:[`Abduvosid Malikov`],affiliation:`BlueThrone`,kind:`lightning`},{start:`11:15`,end:`11:30`,title:`Build an AI call intelligence pipeline on AWS Bedrock`,description:`See how a logistics company replaced a costly AI add-on with a call intelligence pipeline on Amazon Bedrock Data Automation. The session covers call summaries, transcripts and moderation flags, plus asynchronous enrichment, bounded retries and the practical costs of building versus buying.`,speakers:[`Aleksey Melnik`],affiliation:`Imran`,kind:`lightning`},{start:`11:30`,end:`12:15`,title:`Building production-ready AI Agents with Spring AI, Embabel and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore`,description:`Build AI agents in Java with Spring AI and Embabel, connect them to tools through MCP, and deploy them on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime. Explore goal-driven agent flows, OpenTelemetry-compatible observability, Gateway, short- and long-term memory, identity controls, and integrations between Spring AI and AgentCore.`,speakers:[`Vadym Kazulkin`],affiliation:`AWS Serverless Hero`},{start:`12:15`,end:`12:45`,title:`Real-Time Analytics for the AI Agent Era: Building an Agent-Ready Data Platform with StarRocks on AWS`,description:`Learn how to build a real-time analytics platform for production AI agents with StarRocks on AWS. Explore how fresh data, fast queries and high concurrency bring together live streams and historical lakehouse data to give agents reliable context for their responses and decisions.`,speakers:[`Ryan Sun`],affiliation:`Product Solutions Architect, MirrorShip`},{start:`12:45`,end:`14:00`,title:`Group photo & lunch break`,kind:`break`}]},{id:`afternoon`,title:`Afternoon`,sessions:[{start:`14:00`,end:`14:30`,title:`Resiliency meets data residency: How Bank CenterCredit hosts highly available workloads on AWS Outposts`,description:`Explore how Bank CenterCredit built a hybrid platform on AWS Outposts across two geographically separated data centres. Learn how containerized banking applications and databases stay local, integrate with AWS Region services, and support high availability and Kazakhstan's data residency requirements.`,speakers:[`Maxim Geng`,`Aleksandr Bernadskiy`],affiliation:`Bank CenterCredit / AWS`},{start:`14:30`,end:`15:15`,title:`Pure Terraform setup for Enterprise on AWS and how AI can help`,description:`Build enterprise infrastructure across AWS accounts and regions with native Terraform. Learn provider and assume-role patterns, variable organization and repository structures without wrappers or custom scripts, and explore how AI can help.`,speakers:[`Denis Astahov`],affiliation:`AWS Community Hero`},{start:`15:30`,end:`15:40`,title:`How I Fixed Two Dashboard Disasters for Under $10 a Month`,description:`Fix two causes of slow, stale dashboards: manual refreshes and filters that repeatedly scan years of raw CSV. Walk through automated refreshes with EventBridge Scheduler and Lambda, then faster queries with Parquet and Athena partition projection, finishing with the actual monthly bill.`,speakers:[`Aziza Isroilova`],affiliation:`EPAM`,kind:`lightning`},{start:`15:40`,end:`15:50`,title:`Decoupling Serverless Systems: Building Resilient Architectures with AWS SNS and SQS`,description:`Decouple serverless applications and handle high-volume traffic with Amazon SNS and SQS. Learn pub/sub and fanout messaging patterns, along with dead-letter queues and FIFO ordering for more resilient systems.`,speakers:[`Shamshod Isaev`],affiliation:`EPAM`,kind:`lightning`},{start:`15:50`,end:`16:00`,title:`Lambda MicroVM vs AWS Fargate`,description:`Compare Lambda Functions, Lambda MicroVMs and AWS Fargate, and learn when to choose each. The talk breaks down how these compute options differ and where each fits in an AWS architecture.`,speakers:[`Arman Nurgaliyev`],affiliation:`CTO, Freedom Cloud`,kind:`lightning`},{start:`16:00`,end:`16:30`,title:`We Deleted the File That Ordered Our Infrastructure — and Applies Got 2x Faster`,description:`See how replacing a manual ordering file with a trusted dependency graph enabled parallel applies across roughly 14,000 Terragrunt modules. Learn how dependency audits, Open Policy Agent checks and layered GitHub Actions jobs made the change safe, cut average apply times in half, and handled concurrency and AWS API limits.`,speakers:[`Alex Plotnikov`],affiliation:`Staff Cloud Engineer, inDrive`},{start:`16:30`,end:`17:00`,title:`Kubernetes probes: you think you know them`,description:`Revisit Kubernetes probes through a live demonstration on an AWS cluster with a real database and real load. See how familiar YAML settings can cause a healthy service to fail, and learn what to look for beyond a copied configuration.`,speakers:[`Alex Dovnar`],affiliation:`Cloud Architect, DevOps Kitchen Talks`},{start:`17:00`,end:`17:30`,title:`Trust, but Verify: Building Compliant AI on AWS in a Changing Regulatory Landscape`,description:`Explore what compliance means for AI in production and how to build more controlled AI systems on AWS. Learn how to approach trust and verification across AI workloads, use AWS capabilities to support compliance, and adapt to a changing regulatory landscape.`,speakers:[`Mikhail Ruchkin`],affiliation:`CEO, Innovative Digital Transformation`},{start:`17:30`,end:`18:00`,title:`Beyond Structured Data: Bringing Real-Time to Multimodal Analytics on the Open Lakehouse`,description:`Explore how Apache Doris brings real-time analytics to structured tables, JSON, documents and vectors across Apache Paimon, Apache Iceberg and AWS S3 Tables. See how SQL, full-text search and vector search can work together to support RAG and AI agents on the open lakehouse.`,speakers:[`Mingyu Chen`],affiliation:`VP of Engineering, VeloDB`},{start:`18:00`,end:`19:00`,title:`Raffle & closing ceremony`,kind:`ceremony`}]}],Ef=[`radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%,`,`color-mix(in oklab, var(--violet-deep) 20%, transparent) 0%,`,`transparent 78%),`,`radial-gradient(circle at 150% 150%,`,`color-mix(in oklab, var(--magenta) 32%, transparent) 30%,`,`transparent 62%)`].join(` `),Df=`color-mix(in oklab, var(--coral) 62%, transparent)`,Of=Tf.flatMap(e=>e.sessions),kf=new Map(oc.map(e=>[e.name,Of.filter(t=>t.speakers?.includes(e.name))])),Af=[{alt:`AWS Heroes`,badgeUrl:`/badges/aws-hero-mono.svg`,badgeWidth:334,badgeHeight:187,cardIconUrl:`/patterns/aws-hero-pattern.svg`,speakers:oc.filter(e=>e.badge)},{alt:`AWS User Group Speaker`,badgeUrl:`/badges/aws-ug-speaker.webp`,badgeWidth:535,badgeHeight:615,cardIconUrl:`/patterns/iconpattern.webp`,speakers:oc.filter(e=>!e.badge&&!e.featured)}],jf=`/patterns/grain.webp`,Mf=[...new Set([...Af.map(e=>e.cardIconUrl),...oc.flatMap(e=>e.badge?[e.badge.iconUrl]:[])])],Nf=as(`/`)({component:ss(()=>rf(()=>import(`./routes-CbAf9qhG.js`),__vite__mapDeps([12,1,6,7,8,3,13])),`component`),head:()=>({links:[{rel:`preload`,as:`image`,href:jf},...Mf.map(e=>({rel:`preload`,as:`image`,crossOrigin:`anonymous`,href:e})),...[`/fonts/ember-display/common/AmazonEmberDisplay_W_Bd.woff2`,`/fonts/ember-display/common/AmazonEmberDisplay_W_He.woff2`,`/fonts/ember/common/AmazonEmber_W_SBd.woff2`].map(e=>({rel:`preload`,as:`font`,type:`font/woff2`,crossOrigin:`anonymous`,href:e}))]})});async function Pf(){return(await rf(async()=>{let{getIdToken:e}=await import(`./auth-client-BaPj4im9.js`);return{getIdToken:e}},[])).getIdToken()}async function Ff(){return(await rf(async()=>{let{isAuthenticated:e}=await import(`./auth-client-BaPj4im9.js`);return{isAuthenticated:e}},[])).isAuthenticated()}